Package: mc-backup
Version: 1.0.0
Architecture: any
Maintainer: Dylan Bulmer <dylan@bulmer.dev>
Depends: mc-server, ${shlibs:Depends}
Recommends: mc-rcon | mc-mgmt
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://apt.bulmer.dev
Description: Backup and restore plugin for mc-server
 Adds 'mc backup' and 'mc restore', and a systemd timer that runs backups on the
 schedule set in /etc/minecraft/config.toml.
 .
 Archives are written by root into a root-owned 0700 directory and are never
 handed to the service account, which is the one exposed to untrusted mods. A
 restore validates every archive member — names and entry types both — before
 anything is extracted, so an archive containing a symlink, a hardlink or a
 device node is refused rather than unpacked as root.
 .
 Recommends a console plugin — either mc-rcon or mc-mgmt: with one installed,
 the world is flushed and held still for the duration of an archive. Either
 satisfies this, since mc elects one of them and dispatches the backup hooks
 through whichever it picked. Without any console the backup is still taken, but
 of a world that was not flushed.
